From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vates Git Importer <gitimporter@vates.tech>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2015 07:09:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dom0 detects the presence of the ACPI PM timer but cannot
 access it because Xen explicitly denies access. Keep it enabled in case it is
 needed under kexec or for testing native boot but don't detect it for dom0.

---
 arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c b/arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c
index 2f0fa294d617..f71f536d384e 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c
@@ -991,6 +991,9 @@ static int __init acpi_parse_fadt(struct acpi_table_header *table)
 	}
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_X86_PM_TIMER
+	if (xen_initial_domain())
+		return 0;
+
 	/* detect the location of the ACPI PM Timer */
 	if (acpi_gbl_FADT.header.revision >= FADT2_REVISION_ID) {
 		/* FADT rev. 2 */
